<title>USA: WHX sees Q1 loss due to steelworkers strike.</title>
<headline>WHX sees Q1 loss due to steelworkers strike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>WHX Corp said Tuesday it foresaw a loss in the first quarter of 1997 due to the strike by steelworkers at eight of its plants.</p>
<p>The United Steelworkers of America are picketing the plants in Ohio, Pennsylvania and West Virginia, it said, adding that production and shipments of steel at these plants have ceased since October 1.</p>
<p>First Call's consensus among industry analysts foresees a loss of $0.86 a share for the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>WHX reported a fourth-quarter loss of $1.60 against a profit of $0.33 for the same period the previous year.</p>
<p>The strike has yet to be resolved, it said.</p>
